<title>USA: Service Corp Intl issues $450 mln debt.</title>
<headline>Service Corp Intl issues $450 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche debt issue from Houston-based funeral home company Service Corp International was priced Tuesday, according to lead manager J.P. Morgan Securities.</p>
<p>BORROWER SERVICE CORP INTERNATIONAL</p>
<p>AMT $250 MLN	 COUPON 7.375 PCT  MATURITY 4/15/2004</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.695  FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S Baa1  YIELD 7.432 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS  SPREAD 58 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.70 PCT   MATURITY 4/15/2009</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.970  FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S Baa1  YIELD 7.704 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS  SPREAD 83 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
